# Stray Electron user-data accidentally created in-repo by a run with a
# mangled --user-data-dir path (backslashes stripped into one filename).
# The correct pattern (e2e/support/electron-app.js) uses os.tmpdir(); these
# must never be committed.
Users*AppData*/
*-realcopy-*/
.impeccable/critique/2026-07-31T22-34-25Z__src-html-page-map-html.md
.impeccable/critique/2026-08-01T09-10-16Z__src-html-page-map-html.md

# Screenshots from scripts/demo-shots.js — regenerable output, not source.
demo-shots/

# graphify knowledge graph — regenerable output, not source. Rebuild with
# `graphify .` (see CLAUDE.md). ~14MB: graph.json + graph.html are a few MB each,
# cache/semantic holds one file per extracted doc, and graphify writes a dated
# backup folder of the previous graph on every rebuild.
#
# Written as `graphify-out/*`, NOT `graphify-out/`: git cannot re-include a path
# whose parent DIRECTORY is excluded, so the bare form makes the !wiki rule below
# silently do nothing. The `/*` form ignores the contents while still allowing
# git to descend.
graphify-out/*
# …except the generated wiki, which replaced src/docs. It is the project's
# documentation now (CLAUDE.md already points agents at wiki/index.md), so it
# has to be readable from a fresh clone rather than living on one machine.
!graphify-out/wiki/
